{
  "_readme": {
    "what": "Biome fits: replace a structure's own biome list with lists we choose, by what the structure is built from. Each fit below is a biome list AND a structure tag of the same name in structure_tags.json. A structure in the structure tag spawns in the fit's biomes plus the biomes of every fit above it in the path (land/oak structures: land/oak + land biomes), never in a sibling's (a land/spruce structure never gets the land/oak biomes). Its mod's own list is ignored. A structure in two fit tags gets both lists. Structures in no fit tag keep their own list.",
    "why": "Mods list vanilla biomes only (the peaceful watchtowers, most villages and houses: no Terralith biome at all) or every overworld biome (Mysticrift's pillager towers: an oak tower in a dark-oak biome). Two kinds of family: biome-type families (land/plains, land/forest, land/desert...) say what a biome looks like, for villages, houses and ruins; wood families (land/oak, land/spruce...) say where a wood belongs, for structures built of one wood. feature_writeup/structure_tuning.md 3.17 has the per-biome tree table and the family table.",
    "fits": "<name>: {note, biomes: [biome id | #biome_tag ...], inherit}. inherit (default true) = also take the parent fits' biomes; false = this fit's biomes only (land/end). A biome may sit in several fits (forest is in land/forest, land/birch and land/oak). An unknown biome id is skipped with a warning in the log; a missing structure tag or bad entry applies no fit at all (see structure_tag_report.md).",
    "real tags": "Each fit is also added as a real biome tag and a real structure tag, both creativeengineering:<name> (/locate biome #creativeengineering:land/oak works; another datapack can add biomes to the biome tag and the fit follows it).",
    "applied by": "kubejs/server_scripts/worldgen/structure_overrides.js stages the fits to patcherMod worldgen/StructureBiomeFits, which swaps the structure's biome list at world load (generation, /locate, meta structure parts and biome_rules all see the new list). CEConfig [worldgen.systems] structureBiomeFits = false turns it off. Rejoin the world to apply; new chunks only.",
    "rates": "A structure in a group gets more (or fewer) grid slots when its biomes change; python3 tools/gen_structure_groups.py --check shows the new per-biome rates.",
    "open land": "Biomes with no obvious tree go to wood fits by climate: cold (temperature below 0.15, snowy) spruce; temperate oak and spruce; warm and dry or mesa acacia; warm and wet jungle; sand beaches oak, spruce and sandstone, gravel beaches oak and spruce. Overlaps are on purpose (fractured savanna is oak and acacia, forest oak and birch...): more variety.",
    "biome_tags": "biome_tags: biome tags of our own that are not fits ({note, biomes}), added as real tags creativeengineering:<name> by structure_overrides.js; may name fit tags. harsh: for group biome_frequency (structure_groups.json, the vehicles; 2026-10-14)."
  },
